# doc-truth fixture: the `shared/create.tflw` every `import "./shared/create.tflw"` in the guide
# names. It exists so `TF043` (M97c) is satisfied honestly — and, because a readable import closes
# `checkCalls`' world, so that a doc sample calling `create widget(...)` is checked against a real
# declaration instead of being waved through. If a guide page starts calling this with a different
# arity, that page now fails rather than shipping a call nobody could run.
action create widget(name, price)
  api POST /widgets body { name: {name}, price: {price} }
  expect status equals 201
  capture body.id as widgetId
  give widgetId
